  "decisions": [
    "The source Trigger is a Button role combobox, with 32px default/10px corner observed in the native outline Button and 10px popup/4px inset list. Public sm uses an explicit 28px smaller reference role; instance widths 192/256px are not forced. Source Content always inserts a List, so Popup is presentational and the inner List is the actual listbox/aria-controls target; labels remain native field/GroupLabel identities. The Root actual hidden text input is a form/validation proxy, not a second accessible combobox or native select. Default alignItemWithTrigger=true, source collision/scroll-arrow geometry and closing-on-window-resize remain authoritative; fixed mock overlay coordinates are absent. Shared popup surface CSS is explicitly delegated to the common cn-menu-target rule, while option/value/trigger/indicator styles are Select-specific. Source scroll arrows remain decorative pointer affordances rather than invented Buttons. Text/selected arrays, readonly, disabled focusability and independent cancelable value/open transactions retain source behavior; no query input or filtering is invented. Portal direction and theme are supplied on the actual Content element in the adapter.",
    "Semantic token scalar values are meaningful reusable metrics, never coordinate-keyed specimen dimensions. Widths in native specimen grids remain evidence unless explicitly adopted as a domain layout constraint."
  ]
}
